.TH PATSOPT 1 "2026-10-24" "ATS/Postiats 0.4.3" "ATS2 Manual"
.SH NAME
patsopt \- the ATS2 compiler: typechecks ATS source and translates it to C
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B patsopt
.RI [ command " ...]"
.br
.B patsopt \-\-dynamic
.I file.dats
.B \-\-output
.I file_dats.c
.br
.B patsopt \-\-typecheck \-\-dynamic
.I file.dats
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B patsopt
is the compiler of ATS/Postiats (ATS2). It reads ATS source files, checks
their types (including dependent types, linear types and the constraints
they generate), and writes C code. It does not run the C compiler: the
driver
.BR patscc (1)
does that. This line of ATS2 has no garbage collector, and the compiler
rejects every nonlinear heap allocation (a
.B datatype
with a non-nullary constructor, a
.B cloref
closure, a boxed tuple or record,
.B $delay
and
.BR $list_t );
see
.BR patscc (1)
and the documentation below.
.PP
A static file (an interface, suffix
.IR .sats )
is given with
.BR \-s ,
a dynamic file (suffix
.IR .dats )
with
.BR \-d .
The compiler needs the environment variable
.B PATSHOME
to find the prelude and the runtime (the scripts that
.B make install
puts in
.I PREFIX/bin
set it).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-s " filenames" "\fR, \fP\-\-static " filenames
Compile the static files individually.
.TP
.BI \-d " filenames" "\fR, \fP\-\-dynamic " filenames
Compile the dynamic files individually.
.TP
.BI \-dd " filenames" "\fR, \fP\-\-dynamics " filenames
Compile the dynamic files in a combined manner.
.TP
.BI \-o " filename" "\fR, \fP\-\-output " filename
Write the output into the file.
.TP
.BI \-\-output\-w " filename"
Output-write into the file (replace it).
.TP
.BI \-\-output\-a " filename"
Output-append into the file.
.TP
.BR \-cc ", " \-\-compile
Compile into C (the default).
.TP
.BR \-tc ", " \-\-typecheck
Typecheck only; write no C code.
.TP
.B \-\-depgen
Generate information on file dependencies.
.TP
.B \-\-taggen
Generate tagging information on syntactic entities.
.TP
.B \-\-gline
Generate line pragma information in the target code.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable the generation of more informative error messages.
.TP
.B \-\-debug2
Enable the generation of debugging information in the target code.
.TP
.B \-\-atsreloc
Generate a script to help relocate packages in need.
.TP
.B \-\-codegen\-2
Output code generated from level-2 syntax.
.TP
.B \-\-jsonize\-2
Output code in JSON based on level-2 syntax.
.TP
.B \-\-tlcalopt\-disable
Disable tail-call optimization.
.TP
.B \-\-constraint\-export
Export the constraints in JSON format (for an external solver).
.TP
.B \-\-constraint\-ignore
Ignore constraint solving entirely. This is dangerous: use it only with
a proper justification (such as the constraints being solved elsewhere).
.PP
The options
.BI \-DATS " name" [ =value ]
(a top-level definition) and
.BI \-IATS " dir"
(an include path) are also accepted; they are what
.BR patscc (1)
passes on.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PATSHOME
The root of the ATS2 installation (the directory that has
.IR prelude ,
.IR libats ,
.I share
and
.IR ccomp ).
It must be set when
.I bin/patsopt
is run directly.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; non-zero when a source file has a syntax or type error (the
messages go to the standard error).
.SH EXAMPLES
Typecheck a file:
.PP
.RS
patsopt \-\-typecheck \-d hello.dats
.RE
.PP
Translate it to C:
.PP
.RS
patsopt \-d hello.dats \-o hello_dats.c
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR patscc (1),
.BR myatscc (1)
.PP
The documentation of the repository: README.md, INSTALL, doc/GUIDE/.
